# Ilse Varga's camp talks (story/camp_talk.gd): offered after a Long Rest once the opening `if` holds; each plays
# once. Quest: Count Off (narrative/companions/kestrel.dialogue).

# --- After Strahd called Ilse to kneel at the night visit (strahd/visits:night_kneel) ---------------------------------

~ talk_knelt
if name:ilse_varga and flag.strahd_knelt == "ilse_varga"
-> knelt
endif
-> END

~ knelt
Narrator: Ilse is cleaning her greatsword by the fire, the same stretch of blade, over and over.
interject name:ilse_varga: He said fall in. Your company did, at the end. So I fell in. Twenty years of drill, and the first order I obey in this valley is his.
interject name:ilse_varga: That's how he did it, isn't it. My lot. He didn't need swords. He just gave the order.
* Then the next order is yours, Sergeant. -> knelt_order
* You're not on your own in this. -> knelt_alone

~ knelt_order
interject name:ilse_varga: Aye. And it'll be the one he gave them, turned round. Fall in. On him.
-> END

~ knelt_alone
interject name:ilse_varga: I know. It's the only reason I slept at all after. Don't make me say it twice.
-> END

~ talk_fever
if name:ilse_varga and quest.kestrel_company >= the_host and flag.eva_truth_teller != "ilse_varga" and not flag.kestrel_fever_shared
-> fever
endif
-> END

~ fever
Narrator: Ilse has the watch. She also has the letter out again, turning it over and over in the firelight, as if the seal might have changed since the last time.
interject name:ilse_varga: Can't sleep. Don't make a thing of it.
* (Sit with her and say nothing.) -> fever_sit
* Ask about the company. -> fever_ask
* (Leave her to her watch.) -> fever_leave

~ fever_sit
Narrator: You sit. The fire does the talking for a while. Eventually, without looking up, Ilse says the thing she came out here not to say.
-> fever_ask

~ fever_ask
interject name:ilse_varga: I was meant to be with them. Fever. Three days at an inn called the Crooked Mile, a bowl of soup and a great deal of ceiling.
interject name:ilse_varga: I could have ridden on the second day. I didn't want to. Eleven years of other people's wars. I was tired. I let the fever be the reason.
interject name:ilse_varga: They marched. I lay there listening to the rain and feeling lucky. That's the report.
* It wasn't your fault. -> fever_fault
* If you'd gone, you'd be at that table with them. -> fever_died
* Thank you for telling us. -> fever_end

~ fever_fault
interject name:ilse_varga: Didn't say it was. Said it was mine.
interject name:ilse_varga: A sergeant counts heads. Morning and night. I wasn't there to count, and in the morning there was nobody left to count. So. Mine.
-> fever_end

~ fever_died
interject name:ilse_varga: Probably. Forty-one instead of forty. The captain always did like a round number.
interject name:ilse_varga: That was a joke. Don't laugh at it. I'm not ready for that.
-> fever_end

~ fever_end
set kestrel_fever_shared
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: For the record, I'd have stayed in bed too. I'd have stayed a week and complained about the soup.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. Tired is not a sin, Ilse. Not even here.
interject name:silvain_aster: Technically, three days of fever with a measurable temperature is an illness, not a decision. I'd like that noted. Also, I'm glad you were in bed.
interject name:ilse_varga: Noted. All of it. Go to sleep. I've got the watch.
Narrator: She puts the letter away. It's the first time tonight her hands have been still.
-> END

~ fever_leave
Narrator: You leave her to it. Behind you, the letter crackles in her hands for a long time before the fire is the only sound.
-> END

~ talk_count_off
if name:ilse_varga and flag.kestrel_vell_rests
-> count_off
endif
-> END

~ count_off
Narrator: Ilse doesn't sit at the fire tonight. She stands at the edge of the light, the way she stands at the head of a column, and waits until everyone looks up.
interject name:ilse_varga: Count off.
interject name:tamsin_tealeaf: Tamsin. Present, alive, slightly cold.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Hedda. Present.
interject name:silvain_aster: Silvain Aster, present, and I'd like to know what this is in aid of.
* (Answer to your name.) -> count_answer

~ count_answer
Player: Present.
interject name:ilse_varga: Good. Everyone here is present. I'd like to keep it that way. That's all.
if flag.kestrel_roll_kept
Narrator: She opens the captain's roll, finds a name near the middle of the page, and draws a small, neat line through it. Next to it she writes a number: 1.
else
Narrator: She takes out her knife and cuts a small mark into the stock of her sword, beside the hilt, where she'll see it every time she draws. One.
endif
interject name:ilse_varga: One. Thirty-nine to go. As you were.
-> END
